= Labour Chooses Michael Foot

James Callaghan has stood down, and Labour MPs have elected Michael Foot to succeed him, narrowly beating Denis Healey. Foot is a brilliant orator, a lifelong left-winger and a unilateral nuclear disarmer.

The Labour conference has voted to leave the Common Market and to let the unions and party members choose future leaders. The party's right is talking openly about breaking away.
